# The help of a distribution named "Tarantool CLI EE" where tt names
# itself. Regenerate with:
#   go test ./cli/cmd -run TestHelpFlavourGolden -update

=== tt --help
Tarantool CLI EE — utility for managing Tarantool packages and Tarantool-based
applications

[0;1;39mUSAGE[0m
  tt [flags] <command> [command flags]
[0;1;39m
COMMANDS[0m
  backup      Manage Tarantool backups (PITR)
  backup-id   Print an identifier for a new backup
  binary      Manage binaries and SDK bundles
  cat         Print into stdout the contents of .snap/.xlog FILE(s)
  check       Check an application file for syntax errors
  clean       Clean instance(s) files
  cluster     Manage cluster configuration
  completion  Generate autocomplete for a specified shell. Supported shell type:
              bash | zsh | fish
  connect     Connect to the tarantool instance
  coredump    Perform manipulations with the tarantool coredumps
  create      Create an application from a template
  daemon      Perform manipulations with the tt daemon (experimental)
  help        Help about any command
  kill        Kill tarantool instance(s)
  log         Get logs of instance(s)
  logrotate   Rotate logs of a started tarantool instance(s)
  new         Create a skeleton app.manifest.toml in the current directory
  package     Manage tt manifest packages
  play        Play the contents of .snap/.xlog FILE(s) to another Tarantool
              instance
  registry    Inspect the rock servers packages are resolved against
  replicaset  Manage replicasets
  restart     Restart tarantool instance(s)
  restore     Restore a Tarantool cluster from a backup (PITR)
  rocks       LuaRocks package manager
  run         Run the current package under its Tarantool
  start       Start tarantool instance(s)
  status      Status of the tarantool instance(s)
  stop        Stop tarantool instance(s)
  tcm         Manage tcm application
  test        Build the current package and run its tests
  version     Show Tarantool CLI EE version information
[0;1;39m
HELP TOPICS[0m
  errors      Exit codes of tt commands
 
[0;1;39m
FLAGS[0m
  -h, --help                   help for tt
  -I, --internal               Use internal module
      --log-format text|json   Format of the log written to stderr: text or json
                               (default text)
      --no-prompt              Skip cli interaction using default behavior
  -V, --verbose                Verbose output
[0;1;39m
EXAMPLES[0m
  $ tt -V version
  $ tt -I help
  $ tt completion

Use "tt <command> --help" for more information about a command.

